WEBVTT

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:03.163
Let’s walk through Understand the observer boundary.

00:00:03.163 --> 00:00:06.037
Begin by separating access from authority.

00:00:06.037 --> 00:00:09.200
You may inspect the team’s record and follow the exercise

00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:12.287
, but opening, scrolling, or understanding an item

00:00:12.287 --> 00:00:14.912
must never change its workflow state.

00:00:14.912 --> 00:00:17.413
On this slide, this is a read-only view of

00:00:17.413 --> 00:00:19.587
Red Team's Scribe workspace.

00:00:19.587 --> 00:00:23.475
In practice, use visibility to understand the exercise,

00:00:23.475 --> 00:00:26.725
not to assume the authority of an active participant seat

00:00:26.725 --> 00:00:26.887
.

00:00:27.385 --> 00:00:30.198
Before you continue, verify these points:

00:00:30.198 --> 00:00:32.948
Write controls stay hidden or disabled.

00:00:32.948 --> 00:00:36.110
Opening a record does not change its workflow state.
